# Academic Document Benchmark Generator (ADBG) v1.0 — Architecture & Implementation Plan

## Problem Statement & Background

The Academic Universe project currently has a **TypeScript-based synthetic generator** inside `benchmarks/synthetic-generator/` that is tightly coupled to the AU benchmark evaluation framework (Node.js, `pdf-lib`, TypeScript types). It generates PDFs with rudimentary quality overlays (opacity rectangles, rotation restricted to 90-degree multiples), but lacks:

- **True computer-vision-grade degradation** (perspective distortion, motion blur, lens distortion, realistic shadow simulation, noise injection, JPEG artifact simulation)
- **Multi-format output** (only PDF + PNG via optional `pdf-to-img`)
- **Independence** — cannot be used outside the AU monorepo
- **Python ecosystem compatibility** — the broader Document AI research community overwhelmingly uses Python (OpenCV, Pillow, NumPy)
- **Configurable template system** with YAML-driven templates (no-code extensibility)
- **Comprehensive dataset statistics** and scientific reproducibility guarantees

ADBG will be a **standalone Python project** within the AU workspace that can later be extracted into its own GitHub repository and published alongside a Scopus/IEEE paper.

